        "alt_text": "Original textbook mountain and runners photograph"
      },
      "heading": "Altitude"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p0003-b0004",
      "page_number": 3,
      "reading_order": 25,
      "block_type": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "lesson_content",
      "source_text": "Distance from the Sea (Sea Breeze and Land Breeze)",
      "required_for_coverage": true,
      "provenance": {
        "source_line_start": 51,
        "source_line_end": 51,
        "extraction_mode": "markdown_fallback"
      },
      "heading_level": 2,
      "heading": "Distance from the Sea (Sea Breeze and Land Breeze)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p0003-b0005",
      "page_number": 3,
      "reading_order": 26,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "semantic_role": "lesson_content",
      "source_text": "Oceans and seas influence the climate of coastal areas. Water heats up and cools down more slowly than land. During the day, land heats up faster than water, causing a sea breeze to blow from the sea to the land. At night, the land cools down quickly, and a land breeze blows from land to the sea. This keeps coastal areas cooler in summer and warmer in winter compared to inland regions.",
      "required_for_coverage": true,
      "provenance": {
        "source_line_start": 53,
        "source_line_end": 53,
        "extraction_mode": "markdown_fallback"
      },
      "heading": "Distance from the Sea (Sea Breeze and Land Breeze)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p0003-b0006",
      "page_number": 3,
      "reading_order": 27,
      "block_type": "figure",
      "semantic_role": "lesson_content",
      "source_text": "Original textbook sea breeze and land breeze diagram",
      "required_for_coverage": true,
      "provenance": {
        "source_line_start": 55,
        "source_line_end": 55,
        "extraction_mode": "markdown_fallback"
      },
      "media": {
        "source": "images/sea-land-breeze.png",
        "alt_text": "Original textbook sea breeze and land breeze diagram"
      },
      "heading": "Distance from the Sea (Sea Breeze and Land Breeze)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p0004-b0001",
      "page_number": 4,
      "reading_order": 28,
      "block_type": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "lesson_content",
      "source_text": "Direction of the Wind",
      "required_for_coverage": true,
      "provenance": {
        "source_line_start": 59,
        "source_line_end": 59,
        "extraction_mode": "markdown_fallback"
      },
      "heading_level": 2,
      "heading": "Direction of the Wind"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p0004-b0002",
      "page_number": 4,
      "reading_order": 29,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "semantic_role": "lesson_content",
      "source_text": "Winds carry heat and moisture from one place to another. Winds coming from the sea bring rain, while winds from deserts bring dry weather. For example, the monsoon winds bring heavy rainfall to India.",
      "required_for_coverage": true,
      "provenance": {
        "source_line_start": 61,
        "source_line_end": 61,
        "extraction_mode": "markdown_fallback"
      },
      "heading": "Direction of the Wind"
    },
    {
